Subject: [PATCH] Control flow profiler: distinguish branch arms from continuations, and profile && || ??

Bun derives lcov BRDA records from JSC basic blocks, and today that output is wrong twice over:

  1. JSC opens a basic block after every `return`, `throw`, `break` and `continue`, and at the
     join point after every `if`, loop and `switch`. The post-terminator ones are unreachable, so
     they report as branches no test can cover; the join points are not decisions at all. A
     branchless function, fully exercised, reports BRF:3 BRH:2.
  2. `&&`, `||` and `??` are never profiled, so covering a short-circuit arm changes nothing.

This adds `BasicBlockKind { Continuation, Branch }` and threads it from each emission site to the
BasicBlockLocation the profiler hands back, and profiles the logical operators.

Classification is per CALL SITE, not per AST node: a single node emits both kinds. All 28
pre-existing `emitProfileControlFlow` sites were classified individually --

  Branch (10):       ConditionalNode then-arm, ConditionalNode else-arm, IfElseNode then-arm,
                     IfElseNode else-arm, WhileNode body, ForNode body, ForInNode body,
                     ForOfNode body, CaseClauseNode clause, TryNode catch entry
  Continuation (18): ConditionalNode join, IfElseNode join, WhileNode/ForNode/ForOfNode after-loop,
                     ForInNode back-edge and after-loop, after continue/break/return/throw,
                     SwitchNode join, TryNode catch join, both TryNode finally entries, TryNode
                     finally join, program entry, function entry

Eight new sites profile the logical operators (Branch at the RHS, Continuation at the join),
following ConditionalNode's offset convention: `startOffset()` for an arm, `endOffset() + 1` for a
join. The two condition-context variants have no join -- control leaves through trueTarget /
falseTarget -- so they get only the Branch point.

The kind travels in a parallel array on UnlinkedCodeBlock::RareData indexed identically to
m_opProfileControlFlowBytecodeOffsets, rather than as a new op_profile_control_flow operand: the
opcode's shape is baked into the LLInt, DFG and FTL, and nothing that executes it needs the kind.
Only CodeBlock does, at link time. The array participates in the bytecode cache
(CachedCodeBlockRareData) so a decoded block is indistinguishable from a freshly generated one.

ControlFlowProfiler::getBasicBlockLocation caches on (startOffset, endOffset), so one location can
be claimed by several CodeBlocks that disagree about the kind. Branch wins: the kind describes the
source construct, so if any emission of a range is reached because a condition selected it, the
range is a branch arm. Taking the maximum also makes the result independent of which CodeBlock
links first, which lazy compilation would otherwise make nondeterministic.

BasicBlockRange::m_kind is placed after m_hasExecuted, in padding that already existed, so
sizeof(BasicBlockRange) and every pre-existing member offset are unchanged for out-of-tree
consumers of ControlFlowProfiler.h.

NOT COMPILED, NOT TESTED. Written against oven-sh/webkit main by editing fetched copies of the
files; verified only to apply cleanly and to round-trip byte-for-byte.

